## Why This Is Asked

Presents an on-device, multilingual NLP task with concrete constraints (latency, size, privacy) that is accessible to beginners yet touches real-world trade-offs like feature choice, data labeling, and rollout.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference considerations and WebAssembly deployment
- Lightweight feature engineering (character n-grams) and small classifiers
- Multilingual handling with shared subword spaces
- Privacy-preserving data labeling and audits
- Evaluation: per-language metrics, drift monitoring, staged rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight feature extraction prototype
function extractFeatures(text) {
  const t = text.toLowerCase()
    .replace(/https?:\/\/\S+/g, 'URL')
    .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
    .trim();
  const ngrams = {};
  for (let i = 0; i < t.length - 2; i++) {
    const ng = t.slice(i, i + 3);
    ngrams[ng] = (ngrams[ng] || 0) + 1;
  }
  return ngrams;
}
```

